- - - - 1. Height, Weight, Body Mass Index (BMI);
- 2. Pulse and blood pressure including orthostatic blood pressure, when indicated;
- 3. Thyroid palpation and skin exam (acanthosis nigricans, insulin injection or insertion sites, lipodystrophy); and
- 4. Comprehensive foot exam: - a) Visual inspection; screen for PAD (check pedal pulses; refer for ABI if diminished); and - b) Determination of temperature, vibration or pinprick sensation, and 10-g monofilament exam

